**Memo**

To: Investment Team  
From: Sarah Thompson, Chief Investment Officer  
Date: October 5, 2023  
Subject: Quarterly Portfolio Management Review  

As we wrap up Q3 2023, I’d like to provide a comprehensive overview of our portfolio management strategies and asset allocation across various sectors. Our collaboration with BlackRock’s Aladdin system has streamlined our risk assessment processes, allowing us to optimize our exposure to equities and fixed income. Currently, our asset allocation stands at 60% equities, 30% fixed income, and 10% alternatives, with a particular focus on emerging markets, which have shown resilience amid global economic fluctuations.

Our partnership with JP Morgan Asset Management has yielded impressive results, particularly with the Global Equity Fund, which outperformed the benchmark by 3% this quarter, now standing at a year-to-date return of 15.4%. Meanwhile, our allocation to the Vanguard Total Bond Market Index Fund has provided stability, generating a consistent yield of 4.2%, critical as we navigate rising interest rates.

The ongoing collaboration with our risk management team, led by John Martinez, has been pivotal in adjusting our exposure to the energy sector, particularly in light of recent volatility in oil prices influenced by OPEC+ decisions. We have also diversified into renewable energy assets, leveraging insights from our partnership with the International Renewable Energy Agency.

Looking ahead to Q4, I recommend we reassess our allocation to international equities, especially as we monitor developments in the European Central Bank's monetary policy. Our relationship with Fidelity Investments will be crucial as we explore mutual funds focusing on technology and healthcare sectors, which have potential for high growth.

I encourage all team members to review the attached performance reports and prepare for our strategy meeting on October 15, 2023, where we will finalize our approach for the upcoming quarter. Let’s continue to leverage our relationships with organizations like Goldman Sachs and Morgan Stanley to enhance our fund performance and ensure we remain competitive in this dynamic market landscape.

Best,  
Sarah Thompson